    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d832">

                <pb facs="0833" n="575" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg575"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763 72112/1729</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Skinner</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Board Trade decides to make final settlements purchased American cotton not
                    covered by sale contracts, at market value at port of shipment at date of
                    shipment, plus all expenses, including freight, insurance, war risk, and
                    interest. In making settlements actual contracts made about same date will be
                    taken as further guide to arrive at fair price to shippers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Skinner</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
